Build a Modern, Professional Project and Task Management SaaS Application

Act as a senior full-stack developer, SaaS product architect, database engineer, and expert UI/UX designer.

I want you to design and develop a modern, professional, responsive, and fully functional project and task management web application called Trellas, inspired by the best features and user experiences of Trello, Linear, Asana, Monday.com, and ClickUp.

The application should help individuals, freelancers, businesses, and teams organize projects, manage tasks, collaborate with team members, monitor progress, meet deadlines, and improve productivity through one centralized workspace.

The final product should look and feel like a polished, commercially viable SaaS platform rather than a basic task management application or a static dashboard template.

1. PRODUCT VISION AND OBJECTIVES

Trellas should provide users with a centralized platform where they can:

Create and manage multiple projects.

Organize projects into workspaces.

Create, assign, and manage tasks.

Track task progress and completion.

Collaborate with team members.

Set priorities and deadlines.

Manage project schedules.

Monitor team productivity.

Share files and project resources.

Communicate through task comments and discussions.

Visualize project progress through different views.

Manage personal and team workloads.

Receive notifications about important activities.

The application must support both individual productivity and collaborative team project management.

The interface should be intuitive enough for beginners while providing sufficient functionality for professional teams.

